# .env.example — every knob a closed network (self-hosted GitLab, no direct
# internet, corporate proxy + internal mirrors) needs, plus the local-only
# secrets the recipes read, with examples.
#
#   cp .env.example .env        # .env is gitignored; the `wt` helper links it
#                               # into new worktrees
#
# Who reads .env:
#   • just      — `set dotenv-load` in the root Justfile, so every recipe
#                 (pnpm, docker build, docker compose, scanners) sees it
#   • mise      — `[env] _.file = ".env"` in mise.toml, so the mise shims
#                 (node, semgrep, grype, …) see it even outside `just`
#   • CI        — nothing; set the same names as group/project CI variables
#                 (GitLab) or repository/organisation variables (GitHub). The
#                 pipelines only declare defaults, they never hard-code hosts.
#
# Everything below is commented out: the defaults are the public upstreams, so
# an open-network clone needs no .env at all. Uncomment what your network needs.

# ── Outbound HTTP proxy ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Honoured by git, curl, pnpm, mise, docker build (pass-through build args)
# and the docker daemon / dind service for image pulls.
#HTTP_PROXY=http://proxy.internal:3128
#HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.internal:3128
#NO_PROXY=localhost,127.0.0.1,::1,.internal,.svc,.cluster.local
# Lower-case twins for tools that only read these (curl, some Python tooling).
#http_proxy=http://proxy.internal:3128
#https_proxy=http://proxy.internal:3128
#no_proxy=localhost,127.0.0.1,::1,.internal,.svc,.cluster.local

# ── Node / pnpm ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `registry=` in .npmrc does the same for pnpm; corepack needs its own variable
# because it fetches pnpm itself before .npmrc is consulted (the Dockerfiles'
# builder stage and the GitLab jobs both go through corepack).
#npm_config_registry=https://npm.internal
#COREPACK_NPM_REGISTRY=https://npm.internal
# Node tarballs for mise (`mise install node`).
#NODE_DIST_URL=https://mirror.internal/nodejs/dist
#MISE_NODE_MIRROR_URL=https://mirror.internal/nodejs/dist

# ── Container registries ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One variable per upstream registry, used as the image prefix in the CI
# pipelines (`image:` / scanner images) and available to the Dockerfiles and
# compose files as a build arg / substitution. Point each at the pull-through
# cache for that upstream (Harbor proxy project, Nexus docker-proxy, GitLab
# Dependency Proxy for Docker Hub: $CI_DEPENDENCY_PROXY_GROUP_IMAGE_PREFIX).
# `.hadolint.yaml` trustedRegistries must list the same hosts.
#DOCKER_HUB=harbor.internal/dockerhub
#GHCR=harbor.internal/ghcr
#GCR=harbor.internal/gcr
#
# testcontainers-node prefixes every Docker Hub image it starts with this
# (postgres, valkey/valkey, redpanda). Trailing slash.
#TESTCONTAINERS_HUB_IMAGE_NAME_PREFIX=harbor.internal/dockerhub/
# If the daemon is remote (dind, a shared VM) or not on /var/run/docker.sock
# (rootless podman / Docker, OrbStack), testcontainers needs to be told:
#DOCKER_HOST=tcp://docker:2375
#DOCKER_HOST=unix:///run/user/1000/podman/podman.sock
#TESTCONTAINERS_RYUK_DISABLED=true

# ── Vulnerability databases (scanners) ────────────────────────────────────────
# grype: mirror the listing + DB tarballs, or import one by hand
# (`grype db import grype-db.tar.gz`) and switch auto-update off.
#GRYPE_DB_UPDATE_URL=https://mirror.internal/grype/listing.json
#GRYPE_DB_AUTO_UPDATE=false
#GRYPE_DB_VALIDATE_AGE=false
#
# osv-scanner: fetch the offline databases once on a connected host
# (`osv-scanner scan --offline --download-offline-databases …`), ship the
# directory, then point the scanner at it. Consumed by `just sec-deps` and the
# `deps` / `dependency-scanning` CI jobs.
#OSV_SCANNER_FLAGS=--offline --local-db-path /srv/mirrors/osv
#
# semgrep: `p/…` packs are fetched from semgrep.dev. Vendor the rules
# (`semgrep --config p/typescript --dump-config > semgrep/rules/typescript.yml`
# on a connected host) and point here at the directory. Space-separated list.
#SEMGREP_CONFIG=semgrep/rules
# Also stops semgrep phoning home (the recipes pass --metrics=off already).
#SEMGREP_SEND_METRICS=off

# ── mise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Most tools (gitleaks, hadolint, osv-scanner, syft, grype, cosign, k6) are
# GitHub release downloads and semgrep comes from PyPI — mise follows
# HTTPS_PROXY for all of them. Without any egress, run them as pinned images
# instead (the way .gitlab-ci.yml already does); see README "Closed networks".
#MISE_GITHUB_API_TOKEN=ghp_…
#PIP_INDEX_URL=https://pypi.internal/simple

# ── Image signing (local only — CI does not sign) ─────────────────────────────
# `just docker-sign <app> <tag>` reads the private key from the environment
# (`cosign sign --key env://COSIGN_PRIVATE_KEY`); `cosign generate-key-pair`
# writes cosign.key / cosign.pub. Never commit the key — only cosign.pub.
#COSIGN_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN ENCRYPTED SIGSTORE PRIVATE KEY-----…"
#COSIGN_PASSWORD=

# ── Admin server (apps/api, apps/worker) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Bearer tokens for the observability admin server: ADMIN_TOKEN guards the
# mutating /admin/* endpoints (log level, …), DEBUG_TOKEN the /debug/*
# profiling endpoints. Unset = the endpoints are open, which is only acceptable
# when the admin port is not reachable from outside the pod / host.
#ADMIN_TOKEN=change-me
#DEBUG_TOKEN=change-me
